(footprint "Relay_DPDT_Finder-40.52"
	(version 20231120)
	(generator "temper-hand")
	(generator_version "8.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Finder 40.52 series, 2 CO (DPDT) miniature PCB power relay, standard DC sensitive coil, 12VDC (coil code 7.012 per Finder '40 SERIES PCB/Plug-in relays 8-10-12-16A' catalog, cat. no. S40EN, https://cdn.findernet.com/app/uploads/S40EN.pdf, read directly this session): full orderable part number 40.52.7.012.0000 constructed from the manufacturer's own published ordering-code grammar (catalog p.5 'Ordering information' diagram: Series=40, Type/poles=52 (5.0mm pinning, 2 pole), CoilVersion=7 (Sensitive DC 0.5W, catalog p.9 coil table row '7.012': R=288 ohm, I=42mA at 12V, Umin=8.8V/Umax=18V -- the closer match of the two DC coil options to the existing Omron G5LE-1's coil (360R/33.3mA) this part replaces), CoilVoltage=012, then default ABCD suffix (A=0 AgNi contact material, B=0 CO/nPDT circuit, C=0 pin length 5.2mm for PCB or sockets, D=0 standard/non-washtight)) -- '40.52.9.024.0000' (standard-DC, 24V) and '40.52.7.012.0000' (sensitive-DC, 12V, this exact coil code) were both independently found as real distributor listings during this session's research, corroborating the derivation is a legitimate catalog SKU and not fabricated. Body envelope 29(L) x 12.4(W) x ~25(H)mm per catalog p.10 outline drawing (height not critical to this footprint, not independently re-verified). Coil-to-contact-set insulation is stated by the manufacturer as 'Reinforced (8mm)' per EN 61810-1 for BOTH the 1-pole and 2-pole variants of this series (catalog p.6 'Technical data' table: overvoltage category III, rated impulse voltage 6kV, dielectric strength 4000VAC) -- an explicit standards classification, not merely a raw mm figure inferred from a 'clearance/creepage' bullet the way the two single-pole candidates in this project's evidence chain stated it. Insulation between the two poles' adjacent contacts (relevant since both poles are wired in series in this application, see modules.ato BusDischarge) is separately rated 'Basic' (4kV impulse / 2500VAC), catalog p.6. DC1 breaking capacity is given as an explicit manufacturer graph (catalog p.8, 'H 40.1 - Maximum DC1 breaking capacity, Types 40.31/51/52/61', curves for both 'single contact' and '40.52 - 2 contacts in series') spanning 20-220VDC -- read directly at this session's target voltage range (170-200V) and found comfortably above this application's 21.8mA break current on a SINGLE contact already (single-contact curve reads on the order of 0.2-0.3A at 220V; the 2-contacts-in-series curve, used here per the task's requested re-scoping, sits higher still), which is a materially stronger DC-break disclosure than either American Zettler AZ770-1C-12D (30VDC catalog ceiling, 'contact factory' above that) or Panasonic ALZN1B12W (no DC contact rating stated at all) offered. Terminal numbering follows the EN 50005 standard relay convention used industry-wide for general-purpose power relays of this class (A1/A2 = coil; pole 1 = 11 COM / 12 NC / 14 NO; pole 2 = 21 COM / 22 NC / 24 NO) -- corroborated by this session's partial read of the catalog's own bottom-view schematic for type 40.52 ('A1 12 14 / A2 22 24' visible; '11'/'21' COM labels not distinctly rendered by this session's PDF text-extraction but standard for this pin-numbering convention and structurally consistent with the family's 1-pole 40.61 schematic, which shows the doubled-pin form of the same convention). PIN COORDINATES BELOW ARE A HAND-DESIGNED, DELIBERATELY-SAFE LAYOUT, NOT A TRACE OF THE MANUFACTURER'S OWN RECOMMENDED PCB PATTERN drawing (that drawing's exact pitch numbers rendered ambiguously under this session's PDF text extraction, similarly to the two single-pole candidates' own diagrams). Contact-pin pitch (5.0mm) and row separation (7.5mm) are taken directly from the catalog's stated 'FEATURES: 5.0 mm pin pitch' bullet and the 'Copper side view' drawing's labelled 7.5mm dimension respectively; the coil-to-nearest-contact-pin spacing (11mm center-to-center) is a DELIBERATE CHOICE by this footprint's author, sized specifically to guarantee >=8.0mm PCB-surface edge-to-edge creepage from the coil pads to the nearest contact pad (11mm center-to-center - 2x0.9mm pad radius = 9.2mm edge-to-edge, a 1.2mm margin over the 8.0mm target) so that the external board-surface path does not become the governing (shortest) creepage path and silently undercut the part's own certified internal 8mm reinforced rating -- this is the same failure mode this project's own evidence docs flagged for the incumbent G5LE-1 (whose shortest path ran across its own case) and is deliberately designed out here rather than inherited. VERIFY the manufacturer's actual recommended PCB pattern / CAD/STEP file (downloadable from findernet.com for this part) against this hand-built layout before fabrication, per this project's established footprint-authoring convention (see Relay_SPST_Omron-G4A-E.kicad_mod in this same library for the precedent).")
	(tags "relay DPDT Finder 40.52 power relay reinforced")
